* -text linguist-vendored
/hello/core/** -linguist-vendored
# Linguist's include_in_language_stats? only keeps types programming|markup by
# default; 124 of our core languages are type data|prose (Markdown, JSON,
# SQL, CSV, TOML, AsciiDoc ...), so force them detectable/stats-eligible.
/hello/core/** linguist-detectable
/hello/full/** linguist-vendored
README.md linguist-documentation
run.sh linguist-documentation
install_deps.sh linguist-documentation
demo.tape linguist-documentation
LICENSE linguist-documentation
scripts/** linguist-documentation
config/** linguist-documentation
data/** linguist-documentation
logs/** linguist-documentation
assets/** linguist-documentation
.github/** linguist-documentation
*.min.js linguist-generated

# The global `* -text` above means git performs no line-ending normalisation
# at all, so a CRLF artifact written on Windows stays CRLF in the repository and
# a Linux run rewrites it wholesale. That churned hello/manifest.json by 81290
# lines in CI run 37818363260. These last rules re-enable normalisation for the
# file types the generators emit, so the byte-identical content is stable
# regardless of which platform produced it.
*.json text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.txt text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.tape text eol=lf
*.rb text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf diff=python

# The language files are byte-padded to exactly 2048 bytes, so normalising their
# line endings would change their share of the language bar. This rule must come
# AFTER the per-extension rules above, because git applies the last matching
# pattern: with `*.py text eol=lf` listed after this, hello/core/python/hello.py
# resolved to `eol: lf` and would have been silently rewritten on a Windows
# checkout, undoing the exact property the whole repository depends on.
hello/** -text

# Mark our own tooling as vendored so its Python does not compete with the
# language files for space on the bar. The rainbow is the point; the scripts are
# how it is built.
scripts/** linguist-vendored
